Material for help2man(1), which generates the disparPDF manual page, which
also covers disparPDFc, from "disparPDF --help" and "disparPDF --version"
plus the sections below.

[NAME]
disparPDF, disparPDFc \- compare two PDF files textually or visually

[>DESCRIPTION]
.PP
By default the comparison is of the words on each pair of pages, but
comparing character by character is also supported (e.g., for
logographic languages).  And there's also support for comparing the
pages by appearance (for example, if a diagram is changed or if a
paragraph is reformatted, or a font changed).  It is also possible to
compare particular pages or page ranges, and to pair each page of one
file with a page further on in the other, for when pages have been
inserted or removed.
.PP
The differences can be saved as a PDF file, with the pages side by side
and the differences highlighted.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-box ,
only what is inside one of the page boundaries of ISO 32000-2 (the
MediaBox, CropBox, BleedBox, TrimBox or ArtBox) is compared, and the
pages are lined up on its corner, so that, for example, crop marks and
bleed outside the trim box are ignored.  A page without the box uses its
default (the CropBox, or for the CropBox the MediaBox); the box is
clipped to the MediaBox unless
.B \-\-box\-clip
says otherwise
.RB ( \-\-box\-clip
without
.B \-\-box
is ignored, with a warning).  Warnings, such as a missing box or boxes that differ
between the files, go to standard error and into the
.B \-\-xmlResult
file, and do not change the result code.
.PP
In batch mode the appearance of the pages is compared by default, and it
needs no display.  Settings such as the zoom, the tolerances and the
margins to leave out can be given in an INI file
.RB ( \-\-settings ),
whose keys are those of the configuration file (see
.BR FILES ).
.PP
.B disparPDFc
is a link to
.BR disparPDF ,
which, run by that name, is in batch mode without
.BR \-\-batch ,
and shows the window only when given
.BR \-\-interactive .

[EXAMPLES]
Compare the words of two files:
.PP
.RS
disparPDF old.pdf new.pdf
.RE
.PP
Compare them without a window:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ disparPDFc a.pdf b.pdf
0
$ disparPDFc \-\-outType=1 a.pdf c.pdf
1|documents differ at page: 1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compare the words of two files without a window, saving the pages that
differ to
.IR diff.pdf ,
and a detailed result, in XML, to
.IR result.xml :
.PP
.RS
disparPDF \-\-batch \-\-words \-\-pdfdiff=diff.pdf \-\-xmlResult=result.xml a.pdf b.pdf
.RE

Compare only what is inside the trim boxes:
.PP
.RS
disparPDFc \-\-box=trim a.pdf b.pdf
.RE

[FILES]
.TP
.I ~/.config/disparPDF/disparPDF.conf
Settings of the window (layout, zoom, margins, page box, highlighting,
etc.) on Linux and the BSDs, in INI format.  Batch mode does not use
them; see
.BR \-\-settings .
.TP
.I ~/Library/Preferences/com.disparpdf.disparPDF.plist
The same on macOS, as a property list.

